# BRQOSH — Continuous Learning Law v1

**Cloud Code:** `docs/CLOUD-CODE-AGENT-GUIDE.md` · Routes: `LEARNING-INDEX.yaml` · Fable: `R-FABLE-TRI`

**Router:** `.cursor/LEARNING-INDEX.yaml` · **Workflow:** `brqosh-agent-protocol/knowledge-accumulation.md`  
**Quick memory:** `docs/PROJECT-MEMORY.yaml` · **Skill distill:** `brqosh-skills-hub/skill-lessons.yaml`

---

## Core idea

Cursor files are **not** a chat log. They are a **living knowledge base**:

```
Every substantive turn → LEARN phase → principle extracted → routed to ONE primary home
```

Substantive = fix · feature · analysis · decision · mistake · plan progress · new law · failed verify.

**Inquiry-only** (explain with no mutation) → MEM `type: note` only if user asked to remember or new durable insight.

---

## The LEARN loop (every session)

```
REFLECT  — what happened? what failed? what surprised us?
ROUTE    — LEARNING-INDEX.yaml → primary artifact
EXTRACT  — ≤5 lines principle · anti-pattern · verify command
WRITE    — append to target file(s) · never duplicate full text in 5 places
INDEX    — MEM row + skill-lessons if domain lesson · update plan status if applicable
```

Runs **after** VERIFY (or after explicit ⏭ boundary). Same turn when feasible.

---

## Where knowledge goes (never guess)

| Signal | Primary home | Also |
|--------|--------------|------|
| Bug/fix verified | `PROJECT-MEMORY.yaml` | `skill-lessons.yaml` if repeatable pattern |
| Agent mistake / wrong approach | MEM `type: lesson` | `skill-lessons.yaml` + target skill reference |
| New always-on law | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` | MEM `type: rule` |
| Domain how-to (posting, UI, debug) | `skill-lessons.yaml` → domain skill | MEM link |
| Skill workflow gap | Edit relevant `SKILL.md` or reference module | leak-synthesis wave note |
| Active plan progress | `.cursor/plans/*.plan.md` header status | — |
| Plan completed | MEM + extract to skills/rules | mark plan `status: closed` |
| Wave closed | `تقارير/CEEF-*` | MEM · leak-synthesis · STATUS.yaml |
| Architecture fork | `docs/architecture/ADR-*.md` or `docs/memory/` | MEM |
| External deferred | `docs/OPEN_ITEMS.md` | MEM `type: decision` |

**Full routing table:** [LEARNING-INDEX.yaml](../LEARNING-INDEX.yaml)

---

## Per-artifact rules

### Rules (`.cursor/rules/*.mdc`)

- Durable laws only — not session chatter
- One concern per rule file when possible
- Every new rule → MEM + link in `links.rule`

### Skills (`.cursor/skills/**`)

- **SKILL.md** = router + roadmap — keep lean
- **Lessons** → `skill-lessons.yaml` (not bulk append to SKILL.md)
- **Deep patterns** → reference module (`engineering.md`, `reference.md`, …)
- Max **one** synthesis edit per lesson — avoid editing 10 skills for one fix

### Plans (`.cursor/plans/*.plan.md`)

```yaml
# Plan header (required)
status: active | closed | superseded
updated: YYYY-MM-DD
mem: MEM-NNN          # when closed
superseded_by: ...    # if replaced
```

- Update `status` + checkboxes during work
- On **closed**: extract outcome to MEM — plan is history, not truth source

### Memory (`docs/PROJECT-MEMORY.yaml`)

- Every LEARN cycle → at least consider MEM row
- Types: `fix` · `feature` · `removal` · `rule` · `decision` · `lesson` · `note`

---

## Learning from mistakes (mandatory)

When verify **fails**, wrong approach, regression, or user correction:

```
1. Stop — do not hide the failure
2. MEM type: lesson — mistake · root cause · correct approach · verify
3. skill-lessons.yaml — anti_pattern + do_instead (≤3 lines each)
4. If repeated 2+ times → promote to .mdc rule or reference module section
```

---

## Anti-bloat (Fable memory_system)

| DO | DON'T |
|----|-------|
| Extract principle | Paste conversation into skills |
| One primary home + MEM index | Copy same paragraph into 8 files |
| grep PROJECT-MEMORY + skill-lessons before work | "I remember from last chat" |
| Close/supersede stale plans | Leave active plans forever |
| ≤5 line lesson entries | 500-line SKILL append |

